{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST C API.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST C API.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ghost c api blender ghost c api","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST C API.md","fileName":"Blender GHOST C API.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GHOST C API","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender GHOST Windowing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender GHOST Windowing","Blender GHOST Handle","Blender GHOST System Factory","Blender GHOST Window Creation","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST C API.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST C API.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ghost c api blender ghost c api","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST C API.md","fileName":"Blender GHOST C API.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GHOST C API","heading":"Blender GHOST C API","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"GHOST is implemented in C++, whereas Blender's core application is primarily C. The GHOST C API adapts between them by exposing ordinary functions whose parameters and return values include opaque [[Blender GHOST Handle]] types.\n\nEach adapter function casts a handle to the corresponding C++ interface, calls a virtual member, and casts any returned object back to a handle. This lets C callers use [[Blender GHOST System Factory]], [[Blender GHOST Window Creation]], and event services while preserving polymorphic dispatch to the active platform.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender GHOST Windowing","Blender GHOST Handle","Blender GHOST System Factory","Blender GHOST Window Creation","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":"